 and doesn't contribute to any clear pattern.\n\nAfter discarding W9, my hand would be: W3, W3, W6, W6, B2, B3, B4, B4, B5, F2 with better shape for multiple winning possibilities.\n\nReason: W9 is an isolated terminal tile with very limited utility. Only 1 copy remains unshown, making it nearly impossible to form a useful meld. Discarding it maintains my flexible Dots structure (B2-B3-B4-B4-B5) which can form multiple melds, and keeps my Character pairs (W3-W3, W6-W6) which provide flexibility. This maximizes my chances of building toward 8+ points with patterns like Half Flush (6 pts) + Dragon Pung (2 pts) or All Chows (2 pts) + Pure Double Chow (1 pt) + other patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
